- *"I’ll defect to teach them a lesson!"* (They don’t care.)
- *"What if the problem is wrong and they’re not ALL-D?"* (The problem says they are.)

But in game theory, **rational play means maximizing your payoff given the opponent’s strategy**. Since they’re ALL-D, defecting is the only rational choice.

